# Root CA public certificates trusted by the firmware for HTTPS (tools/make_tls_roots.py
# packs their subject names and public keys into src/tls_roots.h). No private key material.
#
# Selected from the Mozilla CA set (certifi 2026.10.23): the roots behind ntfy.sh, Discord,
# Telegram, Slack, GitHub, mempool.space and most public HTTPS endpoints. The "legacy"
# entries (certifi 2024.2.2) are no longer Mozilla roots, but many servers still send
# intermediates cross-signed by them as the top of their chain: the firmware checks that
# top link against these keys (ESP-IDF certificate bundle), so they must stay listed
# until those cross-signatures expire.

